WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
A sprinter explodes out of the blocks.

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.990
Here's a model of her velocity: v equals
three t minus nought point two five t

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.100
squared.

4
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.380
As she runs, the graph of
her velocity draws itself,

5
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.080
second by second.

6
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.750
So when does she stop accelerating?

7
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.350
Never, because she speeds up all race?

8
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.890
Or when her velocity hits zero?

9
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.690
In this mission, you'll see that
when acceleration changes with time,

10
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.780
suvat does not apply.

11
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.280
You need calculus.

12
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.070
Differentiate displacement
to get velocity.

13
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.910
Differentiate velocity
to get acceleration.

14
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.110
And you'll integrate to
go back the other way,

15
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.170
from acceleration to
velocity to displacement,

16
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.580
and find the total distance travelled.

17
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.210
Your mission: find when the
sprinter stops accelerating.
